    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "heading",
    "text": "Arithmetic",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 37,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "When multiplying or dividing positive and negative numbers the sign of the result is given by:",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 38,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "positive×positive = positive positive×negative = negative negative×positive = negative negative×negative = positive",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 39,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "formula",
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{array}{l} \\frac {\\text {positive}}{\\text {positive}} = \\text {positive} \\quad \\frac {\\text {positive}}{\\text {negative}} = \\text {negative} \\\\ \\frac {\\text {negative}}{\\text {positive}} = \\text {negative} \\quad \\frac {\\text {negative}}{\\text {negative}} = \\text {positive} \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$",
    "formula_latex": "\\begin{array}{l} \\frac {\\text {positive}}{\\text {positive}} = \\text {positive} \\quad \\frac {\\text {positive}}{\\text {negative}} = \\text {negative} \\\\ \\frac {\\text {negative}}{\\text {positive}} = \\text {negative} \\quad \\frac {\\text {negative}}{\\text {negative}} = \\text {positive} \\\\ \\end{array}",
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 40,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "The BODMAS rule reminds us of the order in which operations are carried out. BODMAS stands for:",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 41,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "Fractions.",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 42,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "formula",
    "text": "$$\n\\text {fraction} = \\frac {\\text {numerator}}{\\text {denominator}}\n$$",
    "formula_latex": "\\text {fraction} = \\frac {\\text {numerator}}{\\text {denominator}}",
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 43,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "Adding and subtracting fractions. To add or subtract two fractions first rewrite each fraction so that they have the same denominator. Then, the numerators are added or subtracted as appropriate and the result is divided by the common denominator: e.g.",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 44,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "formula",
    "text": "$$\n\\frac {4}{5} + \\frac {3}{4} = \\frac {16}{20} + \\frac {15}{20} = \\frac {31}{20}\n$$",
    "formula_latex": "\\frac {4}{5} + \\frac {3}{4} = \\frac {16}{20} + \\frac {15}{20} = \\frac {31}{20}",
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 45,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "Multiplying fractions. To multiply two fractions, multiply their numerators and then multiply their denominators: e.g.",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 46,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "formula",
    "text": "$$\n\\frac {3}{7} \\times \\frac {5}{11} = \\frac {15}{77}\n$$",
    "formula_latex": "\\frac {3}{7} \\times \\frac {5}{11} = \\frac {15}{77}",
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 47,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "text",
    "text": "Dividing fractions. To divide two fractions, invert the second and then multiply: e.g.",
    "formula_latex": null,
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
    "block_id": 48,
    "doc_id": "6f363b0e46",
    "source": "43799-economics-ff-dl-for-web.pdf",
    "page": null,
    "section": "Economics Facts & Formulae > Arithmetic",
    "content_type": "formula",
    "text": "$$\n\\frac {3}{5} \\div \\frac {2}{3} = \\frac {3}{5} \\times \\frac {3}{2} = \\frac {9}{10}\n$$",
    "formula_latex": "\\frac {3}{5} \\div \\frac {2}{3} = \\frac {3}{5} \\times \\frac {3}{2} = \\frac {9}{10}",
    "image_path": null
  },
  {
